  "reason": "The largest single gain in this study came from switching to multiprofile with avgpool aggregation (+9.5 pts, config_030: 0.632 vs config_028: 0.536), making the aggregation method the most consequential unexplored axis. The only aggregation tested so far is avgpool, which treats all profiles symmetrically. config_032 (scvi_n200, ResNet50, transformer aggregation, concat) is a clean single-variable swap from config_030, isolating whether a learned, position-aware aggregation (transformer) captures inter-profile interactions that simple averaging discards. If transformer significantly outperforms avgpool, it indicates that profile ordering/interaction carries predictive signal and justifies further investment in aggregation design; if it is comparable, it confirms the multiprofile gain is primarily from increased data volume, simplifying the design space. This is the highest-value next experiment because it directly probes the mechanism behind the study's largest observed effect, and the result will inform whether subsequent experiments (e.g., with ViT-L or scGPT) should use avgpool or transformer as the default aggregation."
}

